// pod_borrow_forin_reject.lls — POD-scalar elements and borrows, two diagnostics
// in one pass, each pinned to a different file by the driver.
//
// (1) `for x in &v` over POD elements is screened at the loop itself, so the
//     error lands on the user's own line with an actionable fix.  Before that
//     screen it desugared first and the user got the container's internals plus
//     a cascaded "undefined variable" for the binder.
//
// (2) Calling get_ref directly still instantiates Vec(int).get_ref -> &int and
//     trips the aggregate-only borrow-return rule inside the TEMPLATE.  That
//     diagnostic must name lib/std/core/vec.lls: a template's AST carries the
//     defining file's line numbers, while the checker's source_path during
//     monomorphization is this consumer file.  Mixing the two stamped a stdlib
//     line number onto this file, at a line it does not have.
import std.core.vec

def main() {
    Vec(int) v = [1, 2, 3]
    int s = 0
    for x in &v { s = s + 1 }
    v.get_ref(0)
    @print(s)
}
